      "review_date_formatted": "",
      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "I had problems choosing between Essential Solar and Solar Blast as both quotes were good and the contacts came to inspect the house and both gave me helpful information but I  felt that Solar Blast while more expensive was offering slightly higher quality. 360 Energy seemed to work only from the office and though in your top tier of both panels and inverter, they were at the bottom end and brands I was not familiar with. Jeff Woolnough (Solar Blast) indicated that he was CEC accredited, Solar Blast seems to be a very small business and he showed me how he keeps up with all his installations on his phone. I guess I'm the trusting kind but I think he is honest. He quoted me on 4.6kw of LG panels and then found the panels had been changed. We renegotiated for 5.05kw of LG panels but that required negotiating with Ausnet (over 5kw) and that has held up installation which was no problem to me. I am expecting commencement of installation on Wednesday (13th July) and looking forward to, hopefully, a trouble  free system.Leslie Booth",
